Phở Kim","dish/pho-kim"],["Pho Oregon","dish/pho-oregon"],["Rose VL Deli","dish/rose-vl-deli"],["Shaking beef","dish/shaking-beef"],["Tamarind Tree (restaurant)","dish/tamarind-tree-restaurant"],["The Black Sheep (restaurant)","dish/the-black-sheep-restaurant"],["Tương","dish/tuong"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b0/Ph%E1%BB%9F_H%C3%B2a_Philippine_SM_North_EDSA1.jpg/500px-Ph%E1%BB%9F_H%C3%B2a_Philippine_SM_North_EDSA1.jpg","w":500,"h":348,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ph%E1%BB%9F_H%C3%B2a_Philippine_SM_North_EDSA1.jpg"}},"ingredient/kidneys-as-food":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/kidneys-as-food","n":"Kidneys as food","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The kidneys of animals are a commonly consumed offal. The kidneys can be grilled, sautéed, roasted or braised. They can be used in cooking meat casseroles, stews or pies. Typically used in cooking are beef, veal, lamb and pork kidneys. Chicken kidneys are used in cooking, too, but fowl kidneys are very small and generally not collected to be used in food separately. Veal kidneys are preferred among cooks. The kidneys of small animals are grilled or fried, and the kidneys of larger ones are usually stewed."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kidneys-as-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidneys_as_food"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Brine","ingredient/brine"],["Kidney","ingredient/kidney"],["Liver as food","ingredient/liver-as-food"],["Pearl barley","ingredient/pearl-barley"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/54/Lammnieren-gebraten.jpg/500px-Lammnie